WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:24.360
INFILTRATING ZANSCARE

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.860
"Infiltrating Zanscare".
INFILTRATING ZANSCARE

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:37.900
Darn it, one of them drifted away!

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.800
Quit complaining! I'm doing my best, here!

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.000
All set over here!

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:48.660
I'm moving it.

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:58.060
If we string wires between the rocks and then energize them,

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.030
the Aeneas will just look like an asteroid on radar.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.530
I feel hot again.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.130
But, I still have stuff to do.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.700
I've finished checking underneath.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.730
Portside cables are okay, too.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.030
Warren, how are things on your end?

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:21.800
All finished!

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.900
Martina, can I help?

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:26.130
I'm nearly done over here, too.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.560
Martina? What's wrong?

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:33.030
I'm just a little hot. And dizzy...

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.130
Is it your temperature regulator, or are you sick?

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.830
I've been a little feverish lately, but...

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:40.530
Well, that's not normal.

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.130
Oh! That Warren's snuggling up to Martina again!

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.960
Warren? Martina?

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.760
You're getting too far from the ship!

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.160
Push her into the cabin! Martina's sick!

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.800
Roger!

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.460
How's Martina?

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.200
A little bad. A little bad.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:02.500
It's not a cold, huh?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.360
She needs a doctor.

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.360
Then, let's get her to one!

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.730
Yeah, but...

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:11.500
The nearest space colony is the Zanscare Empire's capital.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:19.430
But Dr. Wattley who lives there should keep quiet about it.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.830
Except, we may be wanted criminals in Zanscare.

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.130
That's true.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.530
Wanted criminals?

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:35.860
Still, if we have to go, then let's go!

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:39.630
Listen, you! Illegal entry's a serious crime! It'd mean the guillotine!

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:40.830
The guillotine...

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.560
Hey, can I have a taste?

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.260
Here.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:06.160
Thanks!

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.000
Leave some for me.

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:11.360
Hey, this isn't a joyride! Get your helmets on.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:12.660
Yes, sir.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.630
They sent us on patrol with no warning, so we haven't eaten.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.500
We need energy!

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:24.360
Yeah. Since the Mutterma Sugan Fleet is facing off with the Side 2 Alliance,

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:28.230
it left our home guard so shorthanded they need us to patrol.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.560
Soldiers who hope to live through an era of warring space states...

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:35.500
...have to get used to this to build their nation.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.630
A rock?

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.260
I didn't get a report on it.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.900
It's just a rock, right?

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.900
That's what it reads as, but...

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:46.330
Uh-oh!

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.860
It's on a collision course with the colony!

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.100
Something that size shouldn't be a problem.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:55.100
If it hits a space colony mirror, the repairs would be a nightmare!

00:04:55.130 --> 00:04:56.030
Move out!

00:04:56.060 --> 00:04:56.900
Roger! Roger!

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.360
Students...

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.160
Patrick, do you read me? Here we go!

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:09.630
Roger. Going now.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.730
It'll look intentional, but that can't be helped.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:20.700
If we use a doll...

00:05:25.160 --> 00:05:27.560
Well, I guess it looks like a mobile suit.

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:32.960
Elisha, should you be up here?

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:35.730
I got her to sleep with some medicine.

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:36.930
Well, Tomáš?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.000
We should reach Zanscare in about an hour.

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:42.860
So, Martina has stabilized?

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.830
Except her stomach still really hurts.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:47.260
I see...

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:49.500
Tomáš, can't we hurry?

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:53.630
I'd like to, but we need to look like a drifting rock.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:56.200
I can't go any faster.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.830
The Gundam's signaling that something's approaching!

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.430
Warren, man the missiles!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.400
What?!

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.260
That's weird.

00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:16.730
It doesn't look like a rock.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.530
Patrick, can you see this?

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:21.000
Verifying. It's a small vessel.

00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:22.730
It sent out dummies?

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:26.500
Be careful!

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:29.300
A regular civilian ship doesn't deploy dummies!

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.930
This might turn into a real battle.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.060
Here it comes!

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:45.330
If it wasn't for the Victory here,

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.500
Tomáš and the others might have been able to talk their way out of this.

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:55.700
Don't accidentally launch any missiles! Got that?!

00:06:56.130 --> 00:07:00.660
Right! We'll just hold off till Üso attacks. Incoming!

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:07.430
The first missile took out a dummy doll! I'm firing!

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:08.360
Not yet!

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:09.330
Right!

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:11.360
Elisha, you sit down, too.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.060
Right.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.900
There's movement like a mobile suit!

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:22.730
Isn't that the white one?! It was disguised as a civilian ship!

00:07:23.030 --> 00:07:24.400
There's just one enemy!

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:26.660
Scatter Minovsky particles and take him!

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:33.200
Just two suits, but with that much firepower? What's going on?

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.560
Warren, launch dummy dolls!

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.230
Roger! Launching!

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:46.660
It's not just one suit!

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:48.330
We're outnumbered!

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:49.960
Nikolai! Brace yourself!

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.130
They're hesitating! It's working!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:57.030
What are you doing?!

00:07:57.060 --> 00:08:00.900
You may be students, but you're piloting Shy-Tarns! Counterattack!

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:06.060
Are the number of enemies decreasing?

00:08:09.330 --> 00:08:10.230
Dummies?

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.430
This style of fighting... Are they guerrillas?!

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.730
Is shooting all they know how to do?!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.100
Did I get him?

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:25.030
What?!

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.730
Pilot, please surrender!

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.160
I don't want to fight you!

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:33.730
The voice of the enemy?

00:08:34.130 --> 00:08:37.800
Pilot, please throw down your weapon and exit your mobile suit.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:42.000
If you don't obey my orders, I'll destroy this suit and the pilot!

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.260
It looks like the infamous white mobile suit.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:46.130
What's he playing at?

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.860
Please, exit the suit, now!

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:52.200
I can't do that unless my superior orders me to!

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.730
Isn't he getting a little desperate?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.430
His combat style's pretty cool-headed, isn't it?

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:00.800
No, without Marbet or Shahkti around,

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:02.030
he gets desperate.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:05.200
What do we do, sir?

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:07.660
Fire a flare to call for reinforcements?

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:10.230
If we do that, he'll kill Nikolai!

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.060
Pilot, please exit the mobile suit!

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:17.700
Okay, we surrender! I'll send out a space boat!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.500
White mobile suit pilot.

00:09:23.530 --> 00:09:24.530
Y-Yes?

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:25.430
I'm coming out.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.230
Please.

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:36.400
Okay, go!

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.260
Go, before he uses that beam saber!

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:39.730
Please, don't use it!

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:44.000
Üso, we'll dash in before a patrol spots us!

00:09:44.030 --> 00:09:45.030
R-Right!

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:48.000
We'll be harder to spot close to the space colony.

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:49.960
Yeah, you're right.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:00.360
This is a space colony?

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:10.060
Over a million people live in this space colony?

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.130
Space colonies rotate at a surprisingly high speed.

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:16.630
We'll need to match that speed to land, huh?

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:25.500
Can we really get inside this space colony?

00:10:25.530 --> 00:10:26.400
We will.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:28.500
Odelo! Warren!

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:31.130
The simulated gravity's going to kick in, so get in your seats.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.060
This will be "down" then, right?

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:36.360
Being under gravity's just going to make it harder on Martina.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.600
Elisha, you get in a seat, too.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.360
Right.

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.360
The gravity's kicking in.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:50.760
She'll be okay. She'll adjust to the gravity soon.

00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:57.530
Üso, I see two ridge bays at 2 o'clock.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:59.460
Sir? Bays at 2 o'clock?

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.300
Üso, hurry!

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:44.030
There was what appeared to be a civilian vessel and a Sinope-type.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:46.700
And the white mobile suit?

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:48.960
And it was powerful!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:51.330
It employed excellent diversionary tactics.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:55.400
And it looked just like one of the old Gundam mobile suits!

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:59.260
What if we used this Sandhoge against it?

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.260
I'll help you.

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:05.100
It's around there, Üso. It should sound different.

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:07.560
There should be a corridor.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.330
I've found the part that sounds different.

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.300
Okay.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:12.130
Bring in the instant airlock.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:15.900
Bring it over to the Gundam's hand.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:17.730
Hold it!

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:18.630
Stop.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:23.500
Even though Üso's never been on a space colony before...

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:25.200
Odelo?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.400
What?

00:12:26.700 --> 00:12:30.460
Stop being jealous of other people's talents. It's shameful.

00:12:30.760 --> 00:12:31.960
All right!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.830
You should play to your own strengths.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:46.930
Once the instant airlock's in place, secure it with birdlime.

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.360
I'm bringing Martina down.

00:12:51.430 --> 00:12:52.530
Please.

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:55.660
I'm worried about Üso.

00:12:56.060 --> 00:13:00.260
I'm wondering if he's getting a little too obsessive in battle.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:02.700
He's not that sort of kid.

00:13:02.960 --> 00:13:06.130
He's an ordinary kid who likes farming and Shahkti.

00:13:06.860 --> 00:13:11.260
Odelo, you should study instead of being jealous of him.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.830
Bring Martina down.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.100
Uh, right! Warren!

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.100
Üso, can you hear me on the contact circuit?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.260
I hear you. What's up?

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:37.460
Something seems to be moving this way.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:40.730
Mr. Václav, I want to do some scouting outside.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:54.400
Can you see it?

00:14:01.860 --> 00:14:03.960
It looks like it may come over here...

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.030
Until we enter the airlock,

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:08.360
maybe you should distract their patrol a little.

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:09.400
You can, right?

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:12.030
I'll try.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:16.600
Shakti's probably on this colony, so I need to get in with everyone.

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:24.300
I'll use the telescopic lens...

00:14:27.030 --> 00:14:28.030
Stop!

00:14:29.030 --> 00:14:31.460
What is that? Checking data.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.860
Not found?

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:45.130
Patrick, do you read me?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.860
Now to put my skills to use!

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:48.200
Same here!

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:52.260
A heavy mobile suit that fires physical ammo!

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:53.300
Don't you see it?!

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:54.500
What, sir?

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:58.560
A light! None of our mobile suits would be out here at this hour!

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.700
Pick up the weapon on your torso!

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:03.400
Mr. Zubroch, please put on a normal suit.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.400
R-Right. Take care of this.

00:15:05.430 --> 00:15:06.400
Sir!

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:09.760
This was our duty to start with! There it is!

00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:15.200
Prepare for hand-to-hand combat!

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:15.900
Sir! Sir!

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.760
Doesn't look like he's running.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:26.630
He probably wants to infiltrate.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:27.560
Okay...

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:29.560
You two operating the arms!

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:33.960
Use the restraining rings on the eight limbs!

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:35.430
We've got this!

00:15:41.060 --> 00:15:42.460
Mr. Zubroch?

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.460
This has been my lifelong dream!

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:49.730
I've always wanted to prove that space colony repair mobile suits...

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.000
...can match up to military mobile suits in combat!

00:15:54.100 --> 00:15:54.960
There he is!

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.300
Don't let him damage the space colony!

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.430
I'll call for reinforcements!

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:05.030
There's no need!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:10.160
He's chasing me.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.460
But I could damage the space colony if I use my rifle.

00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:18.760
There's land with people living on it in there.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:32.100
What?! The beam went out!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:34.600
One more shot, and he'll be immobilized!

00:16:36.830 --> 00:16:38.330
The beam shield can deploy!

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:42.600
The rifle still works!

00:16:43.930 --> 00:16:47.230
That's right! I can't get away from the space colony!

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:54.100
What?!

00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:57.100
Dammit! The monitor!

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.630
I'll show you how the Sandhoge can entangle you!

00:17:10.860 --> 00:17:12.060
Don't use the rifle!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.230
Why not? He's an intruder who's threatening us!

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:17.600
You're not thinking this through.

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:22.560
This machine is a gift from us in the colony corporation, to you.

00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:26.960
This is a chance for you students to be heroes,

00:17:27.000 --> 00:17:32.400
and for me to get machines like this into production!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:33.600
Is it no use?

00:17:33.630 --> 00:17:34.760
It's back to normal!

00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:35.600
What?!

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.930
I won't let you kids disobey!

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.430
Like we're listening to some corporate official?!

00:17:42.460 --> 00:17:44.500
We owe this guy some payback!

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.600
Just because I can't use my rifle!

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:54.830
I'll blow his head off!

00:17:55.430 --> 00:17:56.330
Of course!

00:17:59.630 --> 00:18:01.660
Now we can't use the right leg as a weapon!

00:18:01.700 --> 00:18:03.960
Patrick, give us cover!

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.700
Roger! Take this!

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:08.800
Dammit!

00:18:13.630 --> 00:18:14.900
What do I do?

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:18.260
If BESPA's capital guard shows up, I'm dead!

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.830
There might be people there! I can't risk firing!

00:18:34.330 --> 00:18:36.100
It's working, Mr. Zubroch.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.800
This is the power of my Sandhoge!

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.700
I can still use my rifle!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.400
His rifle's functional?!

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:55.160
Without your limbs... Without your weapons...

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:02.760
So much for you.

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:17.830
Haro, you waited for me?

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:18.860
Haro!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:22.800
Did it break down?

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:27.100
No. Did Mr. Václav and the others reprogram it?

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:28.760
This ball's a stun gun, right?

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:29.830
Haro!

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.500
Dr. Wattley's address.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:35.700
That's where Martina is, right?

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:36.360
Haro!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:40.730
State your unit and mission!

00:19:41.530 --> 00:19:42.700
Haro, stop!

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.260
Here it comes!

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:55.730
Come on!

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:05.430
Company, halt!

00:20:05.860 --> 00:20:07.730
Right face!

00:20:08.730 --> 00:20:13.330
Queen Maria Pure Armonia is headed for the palace!

00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:14.530
Salute!

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:16.300
Wrong place.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:23.430
One, two! One, two! One, two! One, two!

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:25.560
What's wrong, Üso?

00:20:26.030 --> 00:20:31.000
Wasn't Ameria a free colony before it became Zanscare?

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:35.800
You should enlist in the military as well, kid.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.100
I will. Thank you, sir.

00:20:38.230 --> 00:20:39.960
For Zanscare!

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:47.900
Hey. Good job.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:49.060
It's here?

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.130
Yeah.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:55.230
Is the Zanscare Empire a totally militaristic state?

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:56.530
It's terrible, isn't it?

00:21:04.130 --> 00:21:06.300
Now, that's what you'd expect of the former Ameria colony.

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.760
You even see ladies like her coming and going in this part of town.

00:21:09.960 --> 00:21:10.960
Yeah.

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:13.700
Odelo! Oh, and Üso came, too?

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:14.530
Yeah.

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.260
Looks like they took care of Martina's appendix.

00:21:17.300 --> 00:21:19.130
So, we can leave?

00:21:19.160 --> 00:21:21.260
They say she has to be hospitalized for a while.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:23.530
Flanders?!

00:21:25.760 --> 00:21:26.730
Flanders!

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.100
Haro! Haro! Haro!

00:21:28.130 --> 00:21:29.860
What are you doing here?!

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.700
What's Flanders doing in a place like this?

00:21:33.130 --> 00:21:34.260
Flanders...

00:21:35.260 --> 00:21:36.400
Suzy...

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.860
And Karlmann... Suzy!

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:49.030
Suzy, you're okay! Karl, too!

00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:51.860
Suzy, you're okay, right?! You're healthy, right?!

00:21:52.130 --> 00:21:53.200
Yeah...

00:21:55.760 --> 00:21:58.900
C'mon, don't cry. It's okay, now.

00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:02.030
Yeah! Thank goodness, you're all right!

00:22:05.860 --> 00:22:08.400
Is Shahkti nearby, too?

00:23:31.560 --> 00:23:34.560
I met my mother.

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:37.560
And she's the enemy queen!

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:41.160
Not knowing this, Üso and Shrike Team...

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:44.230
...launch an air raid on the capital of Zanscare.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:48.360
Must I become Üso's enemy?

00:23:49.660 --> 00:23:52.960
Next time, on Mobile Suit Victory Gundam:

00:23:53.000 --> 00:23:55.500
Next Episode THE BATTLE OF THE CAPITAL
"The Battle of the Capital".

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:55.530
Next Episode THE BATTLE OF THE CAPITAL

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:56.730
Please watch it!

00:23:56.730 --> 00:23:58.960
